---
# clang-tidy configuration, used by `make clang-tidy` and `clang-tidy.bat`.
#
# The check set is listed explicitly because LLVM 23 enables only clang-diagnostic-* by default
# and then exits with "no checks enabled".
#
# clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound is disabled: the analyzer models strlen() on a string literal
# as the literal's full length, counting embedded NULs as characters (verified with LLVM 23:
# strlen("ab\0cd") is treated as 5).  That makes it report out-of-bound reads for the NUL-separated
# expected-result lists in test/test1.c, which are correct.
Checks: 'clang-diagnostic-*,clang-analyzer-*,-clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound'
